{
  "comment": [
    "T4e's catalogue (split section 3.2): each part before T4e, its named invariants, the test files",
    "that carry them and the part's own commits on the merged line (groups A to E, #173 to #180).",
    "T4-N4 reverts every T2 and T3 part (split, row T4e): `keep` is what a revert leaves at the head,",
    "tests/, so its invariant runs against the product without the part. T3d2's red-first commit is",
    "its proof harness (without it nothing runs), so its revert is its fix commit, the hard SIGKILL",
    "stops, keeping only the proof file and its runner. T4a to T4d are test tooling: no revert, each",
    "proven by its own planted-mutation cases, `planted`, run unmutated (a T4-P line).",
    "`crossings` names each T2 and T3 part's data-separation cases and what each crosses: one",
    "green under the part's revert fails its line by name, whatever the title says.",
    "See tests/ci/self-test/mutations.ts and verdict.ts."
